<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Absa, UK's Tyser set up two new firms.</title>
<headline>Absa, UK's Tyser set up two new firms.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-07-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Amalgamated Banks of South Africa Ltd said on Monday it had joined forces with London-based Tyser &amp; Co to set up two new companies -- Absa Tyser Reinsurance Brokers and Absa Tyser Insurance Services.  </p>
<p>The company said in a statement the partnership would satisfy the growing international insurance needs of Absa's clients, while also acting as a whole intermediary for local business in its UK and European markets.</p>
<p>Absa Tyser Reinsurance would trade only in South Africa, while Absa Tyser Insurance would operate from London where it would make its broking services available to Absa and its clients abroad.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom, +27 11 482-1003</p>
</text>
